{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"980","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"B. Marlin"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1 second"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The city of Fishtopia can be imagined as a grid of $$$4$$$ rows and an "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"odd"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" number of columns. It has two main villages; the first is located at the top-left cell $$$(1,1)$$$, people who stay there love fishing at the Tuna pond at the bottom-right cell $$$(4, n)$$$. The second village is located at $$$(4, 1)$$$ and its people love the Salmon pond at $$$(1, n)$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The mayor of Fishtopia wants to place $$$k$$$ hotels in the city, each one occupying one cell. To allow people to enter the city from anywhere, hotels should not be placed on the border cells."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A person can move from one cell to another if those cells are not occupied by hotels and share a side."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Can you help the mayor place the hotels in a way such that there are equal number of shortest paths from each village to its preferred pond?"}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of input contain two integers, $$$n$$$ and $$$k$$$ ($$$3 \\leq n \\leq 99$$$, $$$0 \\leq k \\leq 2\\times(n-2)$$$), $$$n$$$ is "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"odd"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", the width of the city, and the number of hotels to be placed, respectively."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Print \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"YES"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", if it is possible to place all the hotels in a way that satisfies the problem statement, otherwise print \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"NO"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"If it is possible, print an extra $$$4$$$ lines that describe the city, each line should have $$$n$$$ characters, each of which is \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"#"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" if that cell has a hotel on it, or \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" if not."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"7 2\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"YES\n.......\n.#.....\n.#.....\n.......\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"5 3\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"YES\n.....\n.###.\n.....\n.....\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"B","problemCode":"980B","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/980/problem/B"}